# L §5.5: the 64 cap is counted "after its with pins": with a1 pinned, 2^6 = 64 combinations are allowed.
# Only the combination with every axis p gives 1 (rule r1); a1 is pinned to q, so the value is 0 everywhere.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

axis a1
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a2
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a3
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a4
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a5
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a6
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a7
  p "p"
  q "q"

def n: int
  rule base = 0
  rule r1 beats base = 1 when a1 == p and a2 == p and a3 == p and a4 == p and a5 == p and a6 == p and a7 == p

ask q1: n with a1 = q
=== expect
q1 [a2 = *, a3 = *, a4 = *, a5 = *, a6 = *, a7 = *]: 0
  pinned: a1 = q
  cut 2016-03-01
